Ladybird places the caret for a point inside an inline-block on the
closest of the box’s own lines, and the other engines do the same. In
Blink, LayoutBlock::PositionForPointIfOutsideAtomicInlineLevel() gives
an edge only for a point outside the box, and otherwise InlineCursor::
PositionForPointInInlineFormattingContext() finds the line. WebKit’s
RenderBlock::positionForPoint() goes on to its own content the same way,
through positionForPointWithInlineChildren(). And in Gecko, nsIFrame::
GetContentOffsetsFromPoint() descends into the box’s content through
GetSelectionClosestFrameForLine().
